WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:03.240
Parliament ke bill ki headlines toh padh li.
You have read the headlines about a bill.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.220
Par bill mein actually likha kya hai,
But what does the bill actually say?

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.420
kabhi woh socha?
Have you ever wondered?

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:07.940
Meet JanSansad.

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.500
Desh Ki Baithak.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.360
A clearer way to explore Parliament.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:15.360
Explore Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha questions,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.960
government responses and available debate records.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.760
Search by topic or narrow down your research

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.700
using member and ministry filters.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.740
Browse a catalog of 4,200 bill

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.240
records spanning from the year 2009 to

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.800
2026.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.660
Explore recorded milestones, identified presenters

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:39.840
and available official document links.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.460
Ask in plain English, JanSansad retrieves relevant

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.940
parliamentary evidence and can generate an AI-assisted

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.100
answer with citations.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.200
Open the source record and check the original

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.600
document with yourself.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.420
Behind each search, the system plans the scope,

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:00.680
retrieves passages and checks the relevance of the

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:01.400
answer.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.540
When no relevant evidence is

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:07.600
accepted, it stops instead of generating an unsupported

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.000
or random answer.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:12.160
The web interface connects to a Python backend

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.300
FastAPI service.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.840
Qdrant supports vector Retrieval, SQLite

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.800
and JSON hold catalogs.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:23.120
While Gemini generates from selected evidence,

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.720
Docker packages the services.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.060
Citizens can explore parliamentary information.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.100
Civil service aspirant can find source material for

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.480
polity, governance and public policy.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.780
Coverage is snapshot based and important claims should

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.220
be always verified.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:41.500
JanSansad.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:42.900
developed by Aryan.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:45.680
Explore the project on GitHub and connect with

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.720
me on LinkedIn or Instagram.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.200
The links are on the screen.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.060
Thank you.